---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Developer Update - June 2020';
const date = '2020-06-01';
const category = 'Development';
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} - Dasher Blog`}>
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <article class="blog-post">
      <header class="blog-header">
        <div class="blog-meta">
          <time datetime={date}>
            {new Date(date).toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
              year: 'numeric',
              month: 'long',
              day: 'numeric',
            })}
          </time>
          <span class="blog-tag">{category}</span>
        </div>
        <h1>{title}</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="blog-content">
        <p>
          It's been a few months since we announced Dasher v6, and we wanted to share some updates
          on our progress.
        </p>

        <h2>Repository Reorganization</h2>
        <p>
          We've reorganized our repository structure to make development easier. The main Dasher
          application repository is now at <code>github.com/dasher-project/dasher</code>, and
          the website has its own repository at <code>github.com/dasher-project/dasher-web</code>.
        </p>
        <p>
          This separation allows us to manage the application and website development independently,
          making it easier for contributors to work on the areas they're most interested in.
        </p>

        <h2>Mozolm Proof of Concept</h2>
        <p>
          We've been working on a proof of concept for a new input method using Mozolm (Model-zoo
          for On-line Learning). This could enable new ways of interacting with Dasher, particularly
          for users who benefit from alternative input methods.
        </p>
        <p>
          The proof of concept is still experimental, but early results are promising. We'll share
          more details as this develops.
        </p>

        <h2>NLNet Milestone</h2>
        <p>
          We're pleased to announce that we've completed our NLNet milestone! This funding has
          been instrumental in supporting the development of Dasher v6, and we're grateful to
          NLNet for their support of open-source accessibility tools.
        </p>

        <h2>What's Next</h2>
        <p>
          Our focus for the coming months includes:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Completing the core v6 rewrite</li>
          <li>Expanding platform support</li>
          <li>Improving documentation</li>
          <li>Building out our test suite</li>
          <li>Community outreach and user testing</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Get Involved</h2>
        <p>
          We're always looking for contributors! Whether you're a developer, designer, writer,
          or just passionate about accessibility, there's a place for you in the Dasher community.
        </p>
        <p>
          Join us on <a href="https://matrix.to/#/#dasher:matrix.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Matrix</a>
          to chat with the team, or check out our
          <a href="https://github.com/dasher-project/dasher" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub repositories</a>
          to see what we're working on.
        </p>
      </div>

      <footer class="blog-footer">
        <a href="/blog/" class="btn-secondary">← Back to Blog</a>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .blog-post {
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0;
  }

  .blog-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .blog-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-md);
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .blog-tag {
    background-color: var(--color-horizon-mint);
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .blog-header h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .blog-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-horizon-mint);
  }

  .blog-content ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .blog-content li {
    padding-left: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    position: relative;
  }

  .blog-content li::before {
    content: '•';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-target-coral);
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .blog-content code {
    background-color: var(--color-horizon-mint);
    padding: 0.2rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-family: 'Consolas', 'Monaco', monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }

  .blog-footer {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--color-horizon-mint);
  }
</style>
